    "body": "# AutoTP: send CPU copies in the first-batch consistency check\n\n<!-- r3 2026-10-15, new PR. Branch peng-fix-autotp-first-batch-check-v1 (worktree\n/fsx/peng/workspace/ds-fix-autotp-first-batch-check) on master 5f266e26d. Found 2026-10-03 in the MiniMax-M3 TP + EP\nstudy (deepspeed-500b-study/minimax-m3-tp-ep/FINDINGS.md, item 6). Job IDs: SOURCES.md. In the first test run the new test failed before reaching the check on both the branch\nand master (\"Not able to determine model policy automatically\": it had no partition_config); fixed. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nWith AutoTP, the engine checks the first batch: tensor-parallel rank 0 sends its inputs to the other ranks of its TP\ngroup with `broadcast_object_list` (`check_dataloader_inputs_same_across_ranks` in `engine.py`), and each peer compares\nthem with its own. The inputs are accelerator tensors, so they are pickled with their device. Each peer unpickles\nthem onto rank 0's device and opens a context there, which stays for the life of the process.\n\nOn MiniMax-M3 with AutoTP 4 on 4 nodes, every TP rank 0 GPU showed 3 other processes holding 524 MiB each:\n1.5 GiB of that GPU lost, and those GPUs were the ones that ran out of memory.\n\nThe fix sends CPU copies. The peers' comparison already moves both sides to its own device\n(`compare_tensors_in_structures`), so the check itself is unchanged.\n\n## Used in large-scale training\n\nThe same change (the same line) was in the DeepSpeed study trees of these MiniMax-M3 runs: all 60 layers (426B) built\nfrom the config (random weights), 4 nodes x 8 H200, AutoTP 4 x AutoEP 8, ZeRO-3, bf16, together with the ZeRO-3\nmaster-copy fix (a separate PR).\n\n| This change | Setup | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| no | 32,768 tokens per GPU, no CPU offload | out of memory in step 2 only on the TP rank 0 GPUs (ranks 0, 4, ..., 28), 1.50 GiB short; each held 3 x 524 MiB of other processes' contexts |\n| yes | the same | out of memory in step 2 on many ranks, not only the TP rank 0 GPUs: the model does not fit at this length without offload |\n| yes | CPU optimizer offload, 8,192 / 32,768 / 65,536 tokens per GPU | trained: 30.92 / 59.16 / 106.32 s per step (mean of steps 2-4), 43.5 / 63.4 / 59.1 GiB peak |\n\n## Duplicate check\n\nSearched open pull requests on 2026-10-15 (\"AutoTP\", \"dataloader check\", \"broadcast_object_list\", \"CUDA context\"): none\nchanges this check.\n\n## The change\n\n`deepspeed/runtime/engine.py`, the source rank's object becomes\n`torch.utils._pytree.tree_map(lambda x: x.cpu() if torch.is_tensor(x) else x, args)` (5 lines added, 1 removed,\nincluding a 2-line comment).\n\n## Tests\n\n`TestTpDataloaderCheckSendsCpuCopies` (2 ranks, AutoTP 2, `tests/unit/v1/autotp/test_autotp_training.py`; every\nweight left unsharded with `partition_type: \"skip\"`, as in `TestTpDataloaderCorrectness`): wraps\n`deepspeed.comm.broadcast_object_list` after `deepspeed.initialize`, runs the first forward, and requires every tensor\nthe source rank sends to be on the CPU; the existing `TestTpDataloaderCorrectness` checks that inconsistent batches\nare still caught.\n\nHardware: 1 node of 8 H200 (driver 580.126.09), torch 2.8.0+cu126, pytest 9.1.1.\n\n```\npytest unit/v1/autotp/test_autotp_training.py -k TpDataloader\n# this branch:                         3 passed\n# master 5f266e26d + only the new test: 2 passed, 1 failed (TestTpDataloaderCheckSendsCpuCopies:\n#                                       AssertionError: ['cuda', 'cuda'], the source rank sent GPU tensors)\n```\n\n`pre-commit run --files` passes on both changed files.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n| Cell | Validated |\n|---|---|\n| AutoTP 2, ZeRO-0, bf16 (test) | yes |\n| AutoTP 4 + AutoEP 8, ZeRO-3, 4 nodes | yes, with the same change in a study tree (see above) |\n| Accelerators other than CUDA | the copy uses `.cpu()`; not run |\n\n## AI assistance\n\nThis change, its test and this description were prepared with AI assistance (Claude).\n\n",
